      "test_id": "ut_where_else_to_search_005",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Checked the reply against the external_links_search fixture (external-links-search-wets-schuylkill). The reply does not contain \"All require a subscription\" as the judge quotes; it labels the two sites \"Ancestry.com (subscription required)\" and \"FindMyPast (subscription required)\". None of the rows the tool returned carries an access field, so that label is not grounded in the tool response. That is why the 2 stands. The judge is wrong that the Schuylkill County Records and Church Records rows appear in the reply; neither does. All 8 built links and year ranges match their tool rows.\n"
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_where_else_to_search_005",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Selection",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Checked the ranking against the test's own criterion: \"rows whose linkText names Civil War or military records should rank first\". Pennsylvania Civil War Muster Rolls 1860-1869 is ranked 1st, and places 2-4 (Veterans Card Files, Veterans Burial Cards, GAR Membership) are all military rows, so the military rows lead as required. Putting GAR 2nd instead of 4th is a preference the criterion does not state. IRS Tax Assessment Lists 1862-1918 is the first non-military row and overlaps 1861-1865, a defensible 5th. The judge misread the order.\n"
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_where_else_to_search_005",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Grounding",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Same ungrounded claim as Correctness: the per-site \"(subscription required)\" labels are not supported by any access field in the external_links_search response. The judge attributes this to an opening sentence and to two Schuylkill rows that are not in the reply, but the defect itself is real. Every built suggestion's linkText and years match its tool row, and the 3 free resources without a prefilled search are correctly listed apart from the built ones.\n"
    }
